  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Instead of tossing a coin, Chef Barinov and Mikhail head to the back room to settle their rivalry with a high-stakes cockroach race: the loser must obey the winner completely. Listen to the race.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Что, мы сейчас обязательно выиграем?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Я дал вам самого лучшего.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Выиграю я — будешь моим рабом.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Хорошо, я согласен на это.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Если выиграю я, ты подчиняешься мне.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Ты и ресторан подчиняетесь мне.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Давай начинай!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "И приготовились все сейчас.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Начали! Давай, давай!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Пошёл, пошёл, быстрее вперёд!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Ну, что я тебе говорил?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ну какое же ты чудовище!",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Что, мы сейчас обязательно выиграем?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'So, will we definitely win right now?' The meaning hinges on 'what' working together with 'to win' in spoken Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Я дал вам самого лучшего.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I gave you the very best one.' Senya anchors the line on 'I', while 'best' completes the thought. Chef Barinov answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Выиграю я — будешь моим рабом.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'If I win, you will be my servant.' In Russian, the idea of 'I will win' flows naturally into 'slave' without extra filler words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Хорошо, я согласен на это.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Alright, I agree to that.' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'well' and finishing on 'this'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Если выиграю я, ты подчиняешься мне.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'If I win, you obey me.' The grammar packs 'if' and 'to me' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Ты и ресторан подчиняетесь мне.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You and the restaurant report to me.' Mikhail anchors the line on 'you', while 'to me' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Давай начинай!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Go ahead and start!' The grammar packs 'come on' and 'begin' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "И приготовились все сейчас.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And everyone get ready now.' Senya anchors the line on 'and', while 'now' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Начали! Давай, давай!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Started! Come on, come on!' The grammar packs 'started' and 'come on' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Пошёл, пошёл, быстрее вперёд!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Go, go, faster forward!' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'went' and finishing on 'forward'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Ну, что я тебе говорил?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Well, what did I tell you?' Mikhail raises the pitch on 'told' to turn the phrase into a direct spoken question. Chef Barinov answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ну какое же ты чудовище!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What a monster you are!' Chef Barinov brings out the contrast between 'come on' and 'which' in a few short words. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
